# SysAdminHCP mail-stack — shared build variables
# Sourced by the top-level Makefile and every build/<component>/Makefile.

# ─── vpopmail / qmail user & group (must match across every component + the panel) ─────────
VPOPMAIL_UID=89
VPOPMAIL_GID=89
VPOPMAIL_USER=vpopmail
VPOPMAIL_GROUP=vchkpw
VPOPMAIL_HOME=/home/vpopmail

QMAIL_HOME=/var/qmail
QMAIL_GROUPS=nofiles qmail
QMAIL_USERS=alias qmaild qmaill qmailp qmailq qmailr qmails

# ─── Component versions (pinned) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# notqmail/vpopmail versions + build approach (source tarball, --enable-incdir/-libdir
# detection, CFLAGS=-fcommon) are already live-verified working on install-ubuntu22.sh and
# staged (not yet live-verified) on install-almalinux10.sh — see mail-stack/build/notqmail/
# and mail-stack/build/vpopmail/, which port that exact logic. Every other version below is
# carried over from the original Copilot analysis (QMAILTOASTER-SELF-HOST-PLAN.md) and has
# NOT been build-tested by us yet — verify each one when its build/<component>/Makefile is
# actually run for the first time.
NOTQMAIL_VERSION=1.08
VPOPMAIL_VERSION=5.4.33
UCSPI_TCP_VERSION=0.88
DAEMONTOOLS_VERSION=0.76
SPAMDYKE_VERSION=5.0.1
SIMSCAN_VERSION=1.4.0
QMAILADMIN_VERSION=1.2.16
VQADMIN_VERSION=2.3.7
EZMLM_IDX_VERSION=0.53
AUTORESPOND_VERSION=2.0.5
LIBSRS2_VERSION=1.0.18
RIPMIME_VERSION=1.4.0.10
MAILDROP_VERSION=3.1.8
LIBDOMAINKEYS_VERSION=0.69
# No independent upstream/GitHub mirror exists for these three — source is vendored (one-time
# fork from QMT's own SRPMs, see mail-stack/vendor/README.md) rather than fetched at build
# time, so the qmt-testing repo is never touched again after the initial vendoring.
CONTROL_PANEL_VERSION=0.5.1
QMAILMRTG_VERSION=4.2
ISOQLOG_VERSION=2.2.1

# ─── Build flags ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: this file is `include`'d directly by Make (not sourced by bash) — no shell-style
# quotes around values. Make treats the rest of the line after '=' as the literal value,
# quotes included, so a quoted value here would end up with literal quote characters baked
# into e.g. $(CFLAGS_VPOPMAIL) wherever it's used in a recipe.
# GCC 14 (AlmaLinux 10's default) made -Wimplicit-function-declaration,
# -Wincompatible-pointer-types, and -Wint-conversion errors instead of warnings by default —
# breaks K&R-style implicit declarations (lseek, read, implicit int, untyped argv, etc.)
# throughout every ~20-year-old DJB/QMT-era C codebase in this build, not just notqmail and
# vpopmail (confirmed live 2026-08-02 in both of those already). Applied to every component's
# CFLAGS up front now, rather than waiting to hit the same class of error 11 more times.
CFLAGS_COMMON=-O2 -g -Wall -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types -Wno-error=int-conversion
# GCC 10+ additionally defaults to -fno-common, which breaks vpopmail's ~20-year-old
# tentative-definition globals (MYSQL_READ_SERVER etc. declared without 'extern' in a shared
# header, linked from multiple .o files) with "multiple definition of ..." at the final link
# step — confirmed live on both Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and AlmaLinux 10. -fcommon restores the
# old behavior. Confirmed live 2026-08-02: this exact combined flag set takes the build from
# a hard compile error to a fully working install (vadddomain/vadduser/vpasswd/vdeluser all
# confirmed not to segfault, real SMTP delivery and real IMAP login both confirmed working).
CFLAGS_VPOPMAIL=$(CFLAGS_COMMON) -fcommon

# ─── MySQL/MariaDB client detection ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Neither AlmaLinux 10 nor modern Ubuntu/Debian ship libmysqlclient.so.24 anymore — only
# MariaDB Connector/C (libmariadb.so.3, headers via mariadb-connector-c-devel / libmariadb-dev
# -compat). This is THE root cause of every prebuilt-QMT-RPM mail outage seen on EL10 so far.
# build/vpopmail/Makefile detects the real include dir at build time (mysql/ vs mariadb/);
# these are just the two candidate paths it checks, not hardcoded per-OS branches.
MYSQL_INC_CANDIDATES=/usr/include/mysql /usr/include/mariadb
MYSQL_LIB_CANDIDATES=/usr/lib64 /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu

# ─── Install prefix used by build/<component>/Makefile targets ─────────────────────────────
# Components install directly to their real runtime paths (not a staging DESTDIR) when built
# via `make install` at this stage — packaging (RPM/.deb, not yet built) will introduce a
# real DESTDIR/buildroot layer later.
